The Realtek source files are pinned in PIErtw88/upstream.json.
PIE selects their BSD-3-Clause alternative. The original files remain
unmodified. The build checks their complete file set, revision, hashes
and explicit licence alternatives before compiling.

The installed licence scanner reports only GPL-2 for these dual-licensed
headers. debian/lrc.config lists those audited originals and two source manifests.
The source manifests trigger content-based scanner false positives.
The build checks their fixed hashes.
debian/check-source-notices rejects extra paths that could match the
scanner's partial-path exclusions. Other source files remain checked.

The regulatory database inputs are pinned separately. Their ISC licence
and hashes are checked when the channel tables are generated.
